{"game": "space-marine-2011", "language": "english", "appid": 55150, "month": "2020-12", "window": 4, "start_date": 1608768000, "end_date": 1609459199, "month_true_total": 146, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-09 17:59:36 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "83678710", "author": {"steamid": "76561197988121364", "personaname": "Professional Nephew", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561197988121364/", "num_games_owned": 761, "num_reviews": 126, "playtime_forever": 371, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 371, "last_played": 1587517597, "avatar": "c293c28982636383df5d1a086ad95c20011158ac"}, "language": "english", "review": "A 6 hour campaign thats good for about 5 hours but falters in the last stretch. For majority of the game you are fighting orks in some absolutely perfect Warhammer 40k combat. Chunky weapons, tons of blood and gibs, heavy melee strikes that shake the ground, this game really sells the space marine fantasy. The problem with the final chapters is they introduce chaos marines and demons as new enemies, which should've been a great escalation! But the chaos forces are not nearly as fun to fight as the orks. The game almost becomes a cover shooter at points, worse still is all the chaos enemies dissolve into piddly puffs of sparkles and smoke when killed instead of exploding into gore! Get on a decent sale and don't worry if you start to lose interest in the last chapter.", "timestamp_created": 1609448025, "timestamp_updated": 1609448025, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "83673325", "author": {"steamid": "76561198310593163", "personaname": "xXxmass", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "h